Z||000002||stimpy||02-28-2001||11:51 AM||||I'll volunteer my thoughts.<BR>Your wiper control needs to learn that while its o.k. to be sensitive, and even to cry now and then, there are people that rely on it and it should show courage in the face of adversity.  I think a lack of cofidence can have something to do with it. Try sharing some encouraging words now and then.  If this proves inffective, perhaps medication will be helpful.<P>Hope I have been able to help. I hate to see a plea for assistance go unanswered.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||02-28-2001||04:13 PM||||I've tried smacking it around and calling it a worthless piece of you know what but it didn't help.<P>Go figure.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||02-28-2001||05:39 PM||||Sounds to me like the wiper switch is defective.  The solution would be to replace the switch which is inside the steering column.  You will need to remove the wheel and lock plate, ignition key cylinder, and turn signal switch to replace it.  <P>I recently purchased a replacement switch from Advance Auto for about $55 (GP Sorensen #DS170).  It is also available from PartsAmerica.com<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||02-28-2001||07:00 PM||||yeah, I'd say the switch is getting crappy.||||reg||1
